{
  "version": "2.0",
  "pipeline_stage": "validated",
  "title": "A multimodal epilepsy dataset of paired 3-Tesla and 7-Tesla MRI and intracranial EEG (Penn 3T-7T, Pennsieve 662)",
  "description": "This dataset contains paired 3-Tesla and 7-Tesla MRI (structural and resting-state fMRI) from 30 patients with drug-resistant focal epilepsy. For 15 of these patients it also provides curated ictal and interictal intracranial EEG epochs, with electrode localization from iEEG-recon. Preprocessing derivatives (fMRIPrep, FreeSurfer, iEEG-recon) are included. It is a NEMAR redistribution of Pennsieve Discover dataset 662.",
  "methods_description": "Patients underwent paired 3T and 7T MRI, including structural scans and resting-state fMRI. Intracranial EEG (ECoG grids/strips and/or SEEG depth electrodes) was sampled at 500, 512 or 1024 Hz. Ictal epochs were selected from epileptologist notes, and interictal epochs were randomly selected under timing constraints relative to implantation and seizures. Electrodes were localized on post-implant CT and mapped to pre-implant MRI with iEEG-recon.",
